      "writtenOn": "2022-05-10T05:48:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So the power_signal_init() code should I still think run as part of the\nSYS_INIT phase rather than waiting for the thread to start.\nThis was deliberately done early.\n\nAlso, setting the initial state of the CPU was also done early so that other code (like the power button code) could check the state of the CPU before this thread started.\n\nI think it is OK to do this since these should use internal functions to set the internal state of the power sequence code, and these perhaps don\u0027t need to be checking the thread state.\n\npwr_sm_set_state should be an internal function, and shouldn\u0027t be invoked from anywhere outside the power sequence code.",
      "revId": "1a1f88280547edeee287f34571c42bd4f4683288",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
